  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "ROUNDUP adds its unit in binary64, one bit from the decimal answer",
  "statement": "ROUNDUP forms the ROUNDDOWN result, converts it to binary64, converts one unit 10^-p to binary64, and adds the two in binary64. The sum need not be the binary64 value nearest the decimal answer, so ROUNDUP(-1.125,2) is -1.1300000000000001 and ROUNDUP(3.535,2) is 3.5399999999999996. The difference shows when the result is compared with a typed 3.54.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Under the family rules the OxFunc-Evidence bank matches ROUND 36,391 of 36,945 rows, ROUNDUP 49,013 of 52,841, ROUNDDOWN 59,080 of 59,995 and TRUNC 50,409 of 51,317, with no row lost and each remaining failure classified in the write-up.",
